-- title:
--   Laurent expansion on the Z-chart and its pole filtration
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $V$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, with associated projective Weierstrass curve $V.\mathrm{toProjective}$; write $\mathcal{P}$ for the quotient of $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass polynomial, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules, and let $\mathrm{OriginChartRing}$ and $\mathrm{ZChartRing}$ be the degree-zero homogeneous localisations of $\mathcal{P}$ away from the classes of $X_1$ and of $X_2$ respectively. Suppose given a ring homomorphism $\Phi : \mathrm{OriginChartRing} \to T[[Z]]$ sending each scalar $t \in T$, viewed in the chart ring through degree zero, to the constant series $t$, with $\Phi(X_0/X_1) = -Z$ and $\Phi(X_2/X_1) = -w$, where $w = V.\mathrm{formalW}$ is the formal series obtained by iterating the Weierstrass substitution. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\lambda : \mathrm{ZChartRing} \to T((Z))$ (Hahn series over $\mathbb{Z}$) such that: each scalar $t$ goes to the constant Hahn series $t$; $\lambda(X_0/X_2)$ times the image of $\Phi(X_2/X_1)$ in $T((Z))$ equals the image of $\Phi(X_0/X_1)$; $\lambda(X_1/X_2)$ times the image of $\Phi(X_2/X_1)$ equals $1$; every $a \in \mathrm{ZChartRing}$ whose expansion $\lambda(a)$ has vanishing coefficients in all degrees $< -2$ is of the form $c_1 \cdot (X_0/X_2) + c_0$ with $c_0,c_1 \in T$ and $c_1$ the coefficient of $Z^{-2}$ in $\lambda(a)$; and every $a$ whose expansion has vanishing coefficients in all degrees $< -3$ is of the form $c_2 \cdot (X_1/X_2) + c_1 \cdot (X_0/X_2) + c_0$ with $c_2$ the negative of the coefficient of $Z^{-3}$.
--
--   This is the Laurent expansion at the origin of the finite chart of a Weierstrass model, together with the statement that the order of pole detects the filtration $\langle 1, x\rangle \subset \langle 1, x, y\rangle$ of functions with poles of order at most $2$, respectively $3$, at the origin — the Riemann–Roch input in chart form, valid over an arbitrary commutative ring. It is used in the identification of isomorphisms of Weierstrass models with variable changes, via the isomorphism between the $Z$-chart ring and the affine coordinate ring $T[x,y]/(\text{Weierstrass})$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_exists_laurent_zChartRing_filtration.lean

